WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.467
-Guys, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.968
This is very exciting.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.067
From the number-1 movie in the
country, "Don't Worry Darling,"

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.434
Nick Kroll is here tonight!

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:08.000
-Oh!
-On our show!

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
"Don't Worry Darling."

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.100
Nick is going to tell us
what it was like to star

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.234
in a crazy drama and also how it
was like being in the movie.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:19.534
Let's get to some news.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.767
Well, guys, with all the
holiday travel being planned,

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:24.434
President Biden has proposed
new rules that would require

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:28.133
airlines to show consumers the
actual price of plane tickets,

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:33.167
including baggage fees and other
extra costs, before they buy.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:37.200
Yeah. Of course, the airlines
all responded by adding an

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.033
"able to see the full cost" fee.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.100
But besides that --
Yeah, airlines will have to show

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.400
all their hidden fees.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.767
Right now, every
credit-card company is like,

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.000
"Don't make eye contact.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.601
Don't make eye contact.
He's walking right by.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.334
Don't look at him."

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:53.367
Of course, out of spite, now the
airlines are being too honest.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.634
Today, pilots were like,
"Well, folks,

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:59.133
this turbulence is
something to worry about."

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:02.434
Listen to this.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:05.100
A new poll found that,
in a potential 2024 matchup,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.667
Biden and Trump
are essentially tied.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.968
Keep in mind the poll
has a 3-point margin of error

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.267
and a 10-point margin of
"These guys are like 80,

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:16.701
let's not get ahead
of ourselves."

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.934
Well, everybody is
talking about this.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.968
Rihanna just announced
that she is headlining

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:30.934
the 2023 Super Bowl
halftime show!

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Rihanna!

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.033
But it's Rihanna,
so she was like, "Wow.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:41.734
This is one of the
top-10 honors of my week."

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.300
You can tell fans
are excited because at

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.033
the beginning of every game,
the announcer is like,

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.901
"And remember,
the winning team advances to

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:50.033
the Rihanna concert."

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.100
And it was just announced
that Apple Music

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.701
has replaced
Pepsi as the sponsor of

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.467
the Super Bowl halftime show.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:59.334
And just like with Pepsi,
the NFL was told,

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:00.534
"We don't have Spotify.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:04.033
Is Apple Music okay?"

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:08.868
Of course, if it rains, Rihanna
will stand under...an umbrella.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.501
♪♪

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:14.234
Or she'll have to be submerged
in a bowl of rice for two days.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:17.467
Since it's Apple.
That's the way Apple...

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.968
During -- Speaking of the NFL,
during yesterday's game --

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:22.901
I don't know if you saw this --
between the Miami Dolphins

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.801
and the Buffalo Bills,
Miami's punter

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.267
had his kick blocked
in a pretty unfortunate way.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.567
Watch this.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.667
-I don't know. This is risky.
And it was blocked.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.434
-Oh, my goodness!
Blocked, indeed.

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.033
Let's see if we can get a...

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:39.834
Oh, it hit the personal
protector, Sherfield.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.033
-Ooh, yeah.

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.767
The refs ruled it a safety
but said it was

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.734
very close to a sack.

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:48.667
-Oh! Whoa!

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.334
-Very close.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:56.300
♪♪

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.434
Well, hey, everyone,
this is very interesting.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.567
I saw that a school in Australia

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:13.267
banned a student for having
an inappropriate mullet.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.367
Good thing we don't have
any rules like that here at

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:19.067
"The tonight Show,"
right, Higgins?

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.968
-Right on, brother!

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.434
Can't lock down these locks.

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:26.534
Bottom up, homey.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:27.767
-I hear that, brother.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.501
The administrators
at that school

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.901
need to take
a chill pill, brother.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.934
-If I went to that school and
they tried to tame my mullet,

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.601
you know what I'd tell them?

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:39.868
-What?

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:43.167
-I'd tell them this, brother.

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.033
-Rock 'n' roll, brother.
Hot damn, brother!

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.434
-Come on! Yeah!

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:08.100
I heard that grocery prices
are skyrocketing due to

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.033
a nationwide butter shortage.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.534
-Ooh!
-It's bad.

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:13.133
At CVS, they moved
the Land O'Lakes

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:16.167
behind a locked display case.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:18.901
I'll be honest.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:20.300
Biden might have
survived the gas crisis,

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.567
but there's no way in hell
he's going to make it through

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:22.567
a butter shortage.

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:24.267
No way.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.033
And, finally, guys,
it's the beginning of the week,

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.334
and I thought it would be nice
to kick off things

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:28.901
with a few words
of encouragement.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.834
It's time for some
"Monday Motivations."

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:31.968
Here we go.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:37.133
-♪ "Monday Motivations" ♪

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:40.067
[ Peaceful music playing ]

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.968
-When you met Taylor Swift,

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:44.467
that was the best day of
her life, too.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.400
Your therapist
thinks you're hilarious.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.100
Go ahead, post the photo
where only you look good.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.100
Your friends will understand.

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.901
When deodorant gets
bought by you, it's like,

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:07.334
"Yes, this will be super-easy."

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:11.968
That spider you just killed?

00:05:11.968 --> 00:05:14.567
He wanted to die.
It was his time.

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:19.868
Your high-school crush realized
they were in love with you

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:22.234
the day after graduation.

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:26.834
And, finally, you know what?

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:28.167
Spell restaurant
however you want.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:31.300
Everyone knows what you mean --
the place with food.

